(3949517, 558531, 60657, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> I can see Schroeder playing this. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks! What a cool compliment :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: I can see Schroeder playing this.  Thanks! What a cool compliment :-)', '2007-07-30 11:59:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3949524, 558845, 67697, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the score! Beautiful photo.  I gave it a 7.  I love the black and white and love all the lines in it.  The angled corridor is pretty cool.  I''m glad you got to take some pics on your "vacation".  :)</td>', 'Congrats on the score! Beautiful photo.  I gave it a 7.  I love the black and white and love all the lines in it.  The angled corridor is pretty cool.  I''m glad you got to take some pics on your "vacation".  :)', '2007-07-30 12:00:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3949526, 558361, 74605, '<td valign="top">Congratulations for being in the top 20.  This has such a wonderful fell to it. Nice lines and color.  Well done.</td>', 'Congratulations for being in the top 20.  This has such a wonderful fell to it. Nice lines and color.  Well done.', '2007-07-30 12:01:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3949542, 558531, 60657, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by slickchik:</b></div><hr/><i> This seems either oversharpened or oof...I can''t decide which one.  <br/> <br/>This might be better if you could zoom in to have the ducks fill more of the frame and crop so the subject is not in the middle of the picture but in the bottom third. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hi Kristin! You are possibly right on both counts. I had my 300mm zoom almost wide open and did use a bit of sharpening (2 stops in DPP/RAW). As for the rule of thirds, I thought that the mass of water was already overwhelming and this would be even more so, placing the ducks in the lower third.... maybe that may have been the way to go... I''ll try to re-crop and see how it looks! Helpful comments. Thanks!</td>', 'Originally posted by slickchik: This seems either oversharpened or oof...I can''t decide which one.   This might be better if you could zoom in to have the ducks fill more of the frame and crop so the subject is not in the middle of the picture but in the bottom third.  Hi Kristin! You are possibly right on both counts. I had my 300mm zoom almost wide open and did use a bit of sharpening (2 stops in DPP/RAW). As for the rule of thirds, I thought that the mass of water was already overwhelming and this would be even more so, placing the ducks in the lower third.... maybe that may have been the way to go... I''ll try to re-crop and see how it looks! Helpful comments. Thanks!', '2007-07-30 12:03:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3949543, 559019, 67697, '<td valign="top">I almost left a comment on this during the challenge but ran out of time.  I gave this a 6.  I love the lighting on the fern.  The detail and texture on the leaves is beautiful.  The only thing I did not like was the blurred out leaf on the right.  It seemed out of balance with all the other leaves.  However, excellent choice for black and white!</td>', 'I almost left a comment on this during the challenge but ran out of time.  I gave this a 6.  I love the lighting on the fern.  The detail and texture on the leaves is beautiful.  The only thing I did not like was the blurred out leaf on the right.  It seemed out of balance with all the other leaves.  However, excellent choice for black and white!', '2007-07-30 12:03:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3949562, 558336, 65319, '<td valign="top">The detail and the DOF are just excellent.  Well done!</td>', 'The detail and the DOF are just excellent.  Well done!', '2007-07-30 12:06:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3949650, 558903, 74534, '<td valign="top">Hey Werner, awesome job! Many many congrats!<br/> <br/>Excellent composition, and the sky works perfectly with the smooth sea and the long exposure. Beautiful colors. Overall, a great image!</td>', 'Hey Werner, awesome job! Many many congrats! Excellent composition, and the sky works perfectly with the smooth sea and the long exposure. Beautiful colors. Overall, a great image!', '2007-07-30 12:27:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3949766, 556763, 30214, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your green Blue! Nice take two! I also like it more than the original, although being first counts a lot. The light and shadow play is much more interesting here.  By the way, if any critique is permitted in post-voting part of comments :P, I like the bottom green much more than the top (which is a bit over-saturated IMO).</td>', 'Congrats on your green Blue! Nice take two! I also like it more than the original, although being first counts a lot. The light and shadow play is much more interesting here.  By the way, if any critique is permitted in post-voting part of comments :P, I like the bottom green much more than the top (which is a bit over-saturated IMO).', '2007-07-30 13:19:48.000000', NULL, 0),
